# Requirements and design notes

## Requirements

- R1. Simulate the configured model and report derived quantities with units.
- R2. Every numerical result is reproducible from config, seed, and the locked environment.
- R3. Numerical accuracy is demonstrated by convergence and conservation checks.
- R4. Physical correctness is protected by dimensional, limiting-case, symmetry, and
  analytic-benchmark tests.
- R5. Results can be compared with experiment using stated uncertainties and metrics.

## Architecture

```text
config (TOML) -> config.py (validated dataclasses)
                      |
        experiment.run_simulation -> model.Model + solver.simulate -> Trajectory
                      |                              |
         provenance (metadata)        analytic / uncertainty / comparison / plotting
                      |
      cli.py (and optional gui/controller.py) call only the public core functions
```

## Model-form and numerical decisions

Record each modelling choice (equation, closure, parameter source) and numerical choice
(method, tolerances, step policy) with the reason and the test that guards it.

## Error handling and logging

Expected failures raise `ResearchError` subclasses; the CLI maps them to exit codes.
Library code logs through `logging.getLogger(__name__)`; only the entry point configures
handlers. No bare `except`, no silent fallbacks.
